{
  "program": "CBTRN03C",
  "caseId": "case15",
  "description": "A zero amount, which blanks every masked column. Both masks make all eleven digit positions Z, and the IBM rule for an all-Z item is that a value of zero blanks the ENTIRE field - so the detail amount is fifteen spaces rather than a rendered 0.00, and so are the page total and the grand total, which are still zero after the end-of-file arm has added zero to them a second time. The decimal point disappears with them. A translation that rendered '0.00', or '+0.00', or that suppressed only the leading zeros and left the point, differs from this case in every one of those three columns.",
